      "side": 1,
      "message": "i am a little confused by the readTrace() calls.  When we have a connection failure, we move the trace over to mLastMileLogForLastFailure - which i think also clears the trace buffer.\n\nThen if we call dump(), we will write out the mLastMileLogForLastFailure and clear out the trace buffer (but that is already empty - or has some stuff from the time between the write and the disable tracing.  This seems odd if we could get a dump call while we are still tracing - the current trace will be logged, but then cleared and then wont we have some odd half-connection attempt logs in the trace buffer?\n\nOn the success side - say we have three successes in a row, then do we keep appending to the buffer?  it seems like the buffer should be cleared when we enable tracing.\n\ni am sure I am making this too hard - so maybe I am just confused. :)",
